# VITE_ configuration is PUBLIC. Never put AI keys, provider credentials,
# gateway tokens, service-role keys, or encryption keys here.
# Hosted browser configuration is managed by the platform.
# A separate development backend needs its own public URL and publishable key;
# copying frontend source does not provision the backend.
# Keep private credentials in server-side secure settings.

# Compute Providers: use the self-hosted backend (backend/providers) instead of the Supabase edge function.
# "/api/providers" works with the Vite dev proxy; in production use the absolute URL of your API.
# See docs/provider-backend.md. Leave unset to keep using the edge function.
# VITE_PROVIDERS_API_URL=/api/providers
